    "outlook": "The Indian market exhibited a mixed close with NIFTY 50 and NIFTY BANK slightly down, while SENSEX eked out a small gain. Despite varied sectoral performance and negative breadth, healthy buying from both FIIs and DIIs suggests underlying support, ahead of today's open.",
    "keyTakeaways": [
      "NIFTY 50 (-0.19%) and NIFTY BANK (-0.22%) saw minor dips, while SENSEX (+0.07%) was marginally positive.",
      "IT (+0.50%) and Auto (+0.35%) sectors showed strength, with HEROMOTOCO (+2.9%) and TECHM (+1.5%) among top gainers.",
      "Financial Services (-0.41%) and Energy (-0.34%) sectors experienced declines, including SBIN (-1.3%) and BPCL (-1.3%).",
      "Market breadth remained negative with 27 advances against 31 declines.",
      "FIIs were net buyers at 480.24cr, and DIIs also showed buying interest at 235.56cr.",
      "VIX closed at 12.74, indicating stable volatility."
